      "writtenOn": "2021-06-29T08:47:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We intend to use format-\u003ereserved to store some information but it will be cleared by memset(format-\u003ereserved, 0, ...)\nThe tracepoint function here do the same thing as v4l2_subdev_call(set_fmt) to replace\tstatements below, \n    memset(format-\u003ereserved, 0, sizeof(format-\u003ereserved));\n    memset(format-\u003eformat.reserved, 0, sizeof(format-\u003eformat.reserved));\n    return v4l2_subdev_call(sd, pad, set_fmt, subdev_fh-\u003epad, format);\n    \nso tracepoint always return a non-zero value(1:success, negative value:fail) to satisfy if(ret) condition and return immediately.\n    \nIn userspace, ioctl(fd,VIDIOC_SUBDEV_S_FMT,...) return 0 for success and return an negative number for fail.\nso the statement \"return (ret \u003e 0) ? 0 : ret;\" is hoping that ioctl can return 0 when v4l2_subdev_call(set_fmt) in tracepoint is success.\n\nBut actually We can just check if ioctl return a \"negative value\" and do error handling.\n  \nint ret \u003d ioctl(fd_, VIDIOC_SUBDEV_S_FMT, \u0026format);\nif (ret \u003c 0) {\n     VLOGE(\"VIDIOC_SUBDEV_S_FMT failed: %s\", strerror(errno));\n     return -EINVAL;\n   }    \n\nso there is no need to write as \"return (ret \u003e 0) ? 0 : ret;\".\nI already change back to\nif(ret)\n   return ret;\n   \nplease review again.",
